{"summary":"All seven amendments should be accepted. Source review confirms real mass-conservation defects and test gaps, and I additionally reproduced both the default closed-system budget drift and the dissolved-feed-residue water-change inconsistency.","votes":[{"amendment_id":"fr-1-98a44473","decision":"accept","rationale":"Verified. In plant_growth.rs and algae_growth.rs, respiration terms are subtracted from biomass, but only senescence is routed to fine detritus. With respiration_dic_rate_mg_c_per_g_per_hour defaulting to 0.0 and no DOC/DON/DIC update tied to these biomass losses, plant and algae respiration currently destroys tracked nitrogen and carbon."},{"amendment_id":"fr-1-ecf150de","decision":"accept","rationale":"Verified. shrimp_feeding subtracts periphyton and fine detritus from their pools and only stores the amount in daily_food_consumed_g. There is no shrimp biomass gain, no excretion, and no waste return path, so the consumed organic matter disappears from the mass budget."},{"amendment_id":"fr-1-051fc201","decision":"accept","rationale":"Verified. The nitrification path conserves dissolved nitrogen, but aob_growth, nob_growth, and comammox_growth add biomass without any assimilatory nitrogen debit from a dissolved pool, while total_nitrogen_mg counts that biomass. The paired decay terms subtract biomass and then discard it, so growth creates N/C and decay destroys it."},{"amendment_id":"fr-1-47cf70c5","decision":"accept","rationale":"Verified. quiescent_budget_state disables light and zeros plants, algae, microbes, microfauna, animals, and detritus, leaving the closed-system conservation tests in a near-no-op state. Those tests validate ledger plumbing, but they do not meaningfully exercise conservation under active biology."},{"amendment_id":"fr-1-21000832","decision":"accept","rationale":"Verified. The total_n_helper_sums_all_pools and total_c_helper_sums_all_pools tests rebuild the expected totals from the same set of fields the production helpers already use. That cannot catch a newly added nitrogen- or carbon-bearing field being omitted from the helper, so a structural coupling test is warranted."},{"amendment_id":"fr-1-d4003f70","decision":"accept","rationale":"Verified and reproduced. Running a default TankState with budget tracking for 24 ticks produced about +1.968 mg nitrogen and +12.300 mg carbon, with nonzero stage deltas from nitrogen_cycle, daily_plants, daily_algae, and daily_microfauna. That confirms the quiescent-only conservation regression does not demonstrate the stated closed-system behavior for the normal simulation path."},{"amendment_id":"fr-1-00193e6d","decision":"accept","rationale":"Verified and reproduced. total_nitrogen_mg and total_carbon_mg exclude dissolved_feed_residue_g_total on the assumption that it mirrors DOC/DON, but apply_water_change scales DOC and DON without scaling residue. In a quiescent 25% water-change reproduction, DOC and DON dropped to 75% of their prior values while dissolved_feed_residue_g_total stayed at 1.1 g, so the mirror invariant is broken."}]}